{
 "name": "campaign_speed_modes",
 "description": "Speed tiers and compile tax (June PR 6658 G0_eager / G1_default / G1_max; Qwen-Image-2.1 max tier, PR 11731 / 11677): speed_mode off (no patches, the bit-identity reference; rule 21), eager (patches, no compile), default (regional compile), max (max-autotune-no-cudagraphs) per model, plus int8 at max and Z-Image-Turbo GGUF Q4_K_M eager vs compiled (the June table's baseline arm). Compile cost is reported separately (rule 4): cold_s = first image with a FRESH inductor cache, new_s = new prompts (Studio recompiles per new text length, ~14 s), steady_s = repeated prompt; compile tax = cold_s - steady_s, break-even images = tax / (off - steady). The per-cell inductor dirs are fresh on the first run only: delete them before re-measuring. The GGUF cells download unsloth/Z-Image-Turbo-GGUF (local_files_only false; pre-fetch it with hf download --local-dir and set DBENCH_MODEL_ZIMAGE_TURBO_GGUF to keep the download out of load_s) and pass base_repo as the local Z-Image-Turbo dir, TODO(verify) Studio accepts a local path there.",
